# RTK (forced)

The `preToolUse` hook rewrites Shell commands (git, ls, rg, docker, kubectl, test, 100+). It fires only on Shell calls; built-in Read/Grep/Glob do not pass through it.

- Prefer RTK-covered shell commands; output comes back compact.
- For long Read/Grep/Glob output, call `rtk read`, `rtk grep`, `rtk find`, or `rtk rg` directly.
- `rtk gain` shows cumulative savings.
- Never bypass the hook for long output; never use it when byte-exact text is needed for a patch.
